      <div id="quizArea">
        <form id="quizForm">
          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What are the 7 sections of every professional website?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Navbar, Hero, Services, About, Testimonials, Contact, Footer</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Only Header and Footer</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Only Hero and Contact</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> Only Services</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. What is Hero section?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> Big heading + Button at top - First thing user sees</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> Footer</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Contact form</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> Copyright text</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. What should you do before coding a website?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> Plan on paper - Draw boxes for each section</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Start coding at once</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Copy random code</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> Skip planning</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. How to make dark mode remember?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> Save theme in LocalStorage, read on page load</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> Only change color, no save</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> Use alert</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> Use console.log</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. How to toggle a class in JS?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> element.classList.toggle("show")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> element.class = "show"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> element.toggle("show")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> element.add("show")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. How to make smooth scroll when clicking menu link?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> CSS: html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> JS: alert()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> HTML: &lt;marquee&gt;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> CSS: scroll: fast;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. What does HTML do in a website?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> Structure - Headings, sections, buttons</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> Design - Colors</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> Logic - Clicks</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. What does CSS do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> Design - Colors, layout, spacing</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Structure</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> Logic</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> Database</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. What does JS do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> Logic - Menu, theme, form check, clicks</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> Structure</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> Design only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. What to check before launch?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> Mobile test, links work, form validation, no spelling mistakes</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> Only color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> Only title</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> Nothing - Launch at once</label></div>
          <button type="button" class="btn" onclick="checkTest(false)">Submit Test - Check Result</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-next" onclick="resetTest()">Try Again</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <div id="scoreBox">
        <h3 id="scoreText"></h3>
        <p id="scoreMsg"></p>
        <a id="nextBtn" class="btn" href="/lesson42" style="display:none">🎉 You Passed! Go to Lesson 42 →</a>
        <br><br>
        <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showLesson()">← Back to Lesson (Unlocked)</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
